cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Liminis"
abstract: >-
  A voxel simulator of a biological ecosystem, built to study the major
  evolutionary transitions. Environment and organisms are made of the same
  substance registry and the same reaction engine; genomes are rule sets rather
  than blueprints; every gram entering or leaving the world passes through a
  named, counted channel.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Artemev"
    given-names: "Pavel"
repository-code: "https://github.com/emevart/liminis"
# doi: assigned by Zenodo on the first tagged release (ADR-019)
keywords:
  - artificial life
  - evolutionary transitions
  - individual-based modelling
  - reaction-diffusion
  - voxel simulation
